'''''Lessons in Chemistry''''' is an American [[period drama]] miniseries created by [[Lee Eisenberg]], based on the [[Lessons in Chemistry (novel)|novel of the same name]] by [[Bonnie Garmus]]. It stars [[Brie Larson]] as chemist Elizabeth Zott who begins hosting her own feminist cooking show in 1950s America.

The series began streaming on [[Apple TV (streaming service)|Apple TV]] on  October 13, 2023, and ended November 22, 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Petski |first=Denise |date=May 31, 2023 |title='Lessons In Chemistry': Brie Larson's Apple TV+ Series Gets Premiere Date |url=https://deadline.com/2023/05/lessons-in-chemistry-brie-larson-apple-tv-drama-series-premiere-date-1235383171/ |access-date=May 31, 2023 |website=Deadline |language=en-US}}</ref> It received positive reviews from critics, and received nominations for two [[Golden Globe Awards]], [[Golden Globe Award for Best Limited or Anthology Series or Television Film|Best Limited or Anthology Series]] and [[Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Miniseries or Television Film|Best Actress – Miniseries]] for Larson.<ref name="ggnom23">{{cite web |last1=Hipes |first1=Patrick |title=Golden Globe Nominations: 'Barbie', 'Oppenheimer' Top Movie List; 'Succession' Leads Way In TV |url=https://deadline.com/2023/12/golden-globe-nominations-2024-1235660995/ |website=Deadline Hollywood |access-date=December 11, 2023 |date=December 11, 2023}}</ref> In 2024 [[Sarah Adina Smith]] won the [[Directors Guild of America Award for Outstanding Directing – Miniseries or TV Film|Directors Guild of America Award for Outstanding Directorial Achievement in Movies for Television and Limited Series]] for directing the second episode "Her and Him".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/2024-dga-awards-winners-list-1235821741/|title=DGA Awards: Winners List (Updating Live)|first1=Hilary Lewis, Tyler Coates, Kirsten|last1=Chuba|first2=Hilary|last2=Lewis|first3=Tyler|last3=Coates|first4=Kirsten|last4=Chuba|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |date=February 11, 2024}}</ref>

{{Short description|Study of spatial information}}
{{good article}}
{{Geography sidebar}}

'''Technical geography''' is the branch of [[geography]] that involves using, studying, and creating tools to obtain, analyze, interpret, understand, and communicate [[spatial information]].<ref name="Haidu1">{{cite journal |last1=Haidu |first1=Ionel |title=What is Technical Geography – a letter from the editor |journal=Geographia Technica |date=2016 |volume=11 |issue=1 |pages=1–5 |doi=10.21163/GT_2016.111.01|doi-access=free |bibcode=2016GeogT..11....1H }}</ref><ref name="Sala1">{{cite book |last1=Sala |first1=Maria |title=Geography Volume I |date=2009 |publisher=[[Encyclopedia of Life Support Systems|EOLSS]] UNESCO |location=Oxford, United Kingdom |pages = 2, 3, 8, 32, 109|isbn=978-1-84826-960-6 |edition=1}}</ref><ref name="Tambassi">{{cite book |last1=Tambassi |first1=Timothy |title=The Philosophy of Geo-Ontologies |date=2021 |publisher=Springer |pages = 98, 103 |isbn=978-3-030-78144-6 |edition=2}}</ref> The spatial data types a technical geographer employs may vary widely, including human and physical geography topics, with the common thread being the techniques and philosophies employed.<ref name="Arabi1">{{cite journal |last1=Arabi |first1=Mouhaman |last2=Ngwa |first2=Moise |title=Modeling the Relationship Between Weather Parameters and Cholera in the City of Maroua, Far North Region, Cameroon |journal=[[Geographia Technica]] |date=March 2019 |volume=14(1):1–13 |issue=1 |pages=1–13 |doi=10.21163/GT_2019.141.01|doi-access=free |bibcode=2019GeogT..14....1A }}</ref><ref>{{cite book |last1=Boehm |first1=Richard G. |last2=Peters |first2=Samantha |title=Careers/Jobs in Geography:Business Cards of Department Graduates |date=2008 |publisher=Texas State University San Marcos |edition=sixth |url=https://gato-docs.its.txst.edu/jcr:8b8ecd11-661f-4626-8bcb-0e2fe31ed47e/Geography%20Alumni%20Business%20Card%20Directory%20-%206th%20Edition.pdf |access-date=8 November 2023}}</ref> To accomplish this, technical geographers often create their own software or scripts, which can then be applied more broadly by others.<ref name="Kretzschmar1">{{cite book |last1=Kretzschmar Jr. |first1=William A. |editor1-last=Schlüter |editor1-first=Julia |editor2-last=Krug |editor2-first=Manfred |title=Research Methods in Language Variation and Change: Computer mapping of language data |date= 24 October 2013 |publisher=Cambridge University Press |isbn=9781107469846 |page=53}}</ref> They may also explore applying techniques developed for one application to another unrelated topic, such as applying [[Kriging]], originally developed for mining, to disciplines as diverse as real-estate prices.<ref name="Monmonier1" /><ref name="Chilès1">{{cite book |last1=Chilès |first1=Jean-Paul |last2=Desassis |first2=Nicolas |editor1-last=Sagar |editor1-first=B. S. Daya |editor2-last=Agterberg |editor2-first=Frits |editor3-last=Cheng |editor3-first=Qiuming |url=https://library.oapen.org/handle/20.500.12657/22939|title=Handbook of Mathematical Geosciences |date=2018 |publisher=SpringerOpen |isbn=978-3-319-78998-9 |page=589 |chapter=29 Fifty Years of Kriging}}{{open access}}</ref> Further, a technical geographer may explore the relationship between the spatial technology and the end users to improve upon the technology and better understand the impact of the technology on human behavior.<ref name="Lin1">{{cite journal |last1=Lin |first1=Yuancheng |last2=Wang |first2=Min |last3=Lei |first3=Junchao |last4=He |first4=Huiyan |title=Perception and Interaction of Urban Medical Space from the Perspective of Technical Geography: A Case Study of Guangzhou, China |journal=Journal of Urban Planning and Development |date=3 August 2023 |volume=149 |issue=4 |article-number=05023032 |doi=10.1061/JUPDDM.UPENG-4432|s2cid=260653708 }}</ref> 

[[File:BranchesOfGeography.png|thumb|The relationship between the three branches of geography]]
The other branches of geography, most commonly limited to [[human geography]] and [[physical geography]], make extensive use of technical geographies concepts and techniques.<ref name="Sala1" /><ref name="Tambassi" /><ref name="Drake1">{{cite journal |last1=Drake |first1=Dawn M. |last2=Elias |first2=Ashley |last3=Ganong |first3=Carissa |last4=Grantham |first4=Michael L. |last5=Mills |first5=Mark S. |title=Transforming the Applied Learning Experience Through Interdisciplinary Fieldwork |journal=The Geographical Bulletin |date=May 2022 |volume=63 |issue=2 |url=https://gammathetaupsilon.org/the-geographical-bulletin/2020s/volume63-2/article2.pdf |access-date=4 August 2023 |issn=2163-5900}}</ref> Nevertheless, the methods and theory are distinct, and a technical geographer may be more concerned with the technological and theoretical concepts than the nature of the data.<ref name="Sala1" /><ref name="cave1">{{cite book |last1=Cave |first1=Edward |title=Geography reformed: a new system of general geography, according to an accurate analysis of the science in four parts. The whole illustrated with notes. |date=1749 |publisher=Edward Cave |location=London |edition=2}}</ref>  In teaching technical geography, instructors often rely on examples from human and physical geography to explain theoretical concepts.<ref name="Holler1">{{cite journal |last1=Holler |first1=Joseph |title=Human Geography with Open Gis as a Transformative Introductory Higher Education Course |journal=The International Archives of the Photogrammetry, Remote Sensing and Spatial Information Sciences |date=2019 |volume=4214 |pages=99–106 |doi=10.5194/isprs-archives-XLII-4-W14-99-2019 |bibcode=2019ISPAr4214...99H |doi-access=free }}</ref> While technical geography mostly works with quantitative data, the techniques and technology can be applied to [[qualitative geography]], differentiating it from [[quantitative geography]].<ref name="Haidu1" /> Within the branch of technical geography are the major and overlapping subbranches of [[geographic information science]], [[geomatics]], and [[geoinformatics]].<ref name="Sala1" /><ref name="Bello2023" /><ref name="Vega2026">{{cite book |last1=Vega |first1=Ángela Quintana |title=Sciencegramers |date=10 January 2026 |publisher=Springer |isbn=978-3-032-03811-1 |pages=177–212 |chapter-url=https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-03811-1_6 |access-date=5 May 2026 |chapter=Plants, Environment, Animals |doi=10.1007/978-3-032-03811-1_6 }}</ref>

'''World history''' or '''history of the world''' usually refers to [[human history]], the history of human beings that takes a human perspective.

